ch against the shipped `[Verb(\"…\")]` attributes and their `VerbArgs` reads\n   in `Source/AutoRimmer/`. **An item that queries a verb or argument that does\n   not exist is dead on arrival**, and it will look fine forever.\n2. **Does every cited game member exist and say what is claimed?** Check by\n   MEMBER NAME against the decompiled tree at\n   `misc/rimworld/reference/decompiled/RimWorldBase/`, never by line offset.\n   Two specific claims are load-bearing and should be re-derived from scratch\n   rather than trusted: `Alert_LowFood`'s 150,000-tick muzzle (claimed to use\n   `TicksGame`, not `GenDate.DaysPassed`), and the food-days arithmetic that\n   depends on a colonist eating ~1.6 nutrition/day.\n3. **Is every invented number marked?** The convention the authors adopted is\n   `(proposed)` on any threshold not derived from source. Find any bare number\n   presented as though it were derived. Same for\n   `combat-role-passion-over-skill`'s formula, which MUST stay marked as the\n   orchestrator's proposal and not as Evan's rule.\n4. **Does anything assume unbuilt capability?** 3.5 (dialog/quest) and 3.6\n   (bills/storage) are IN FLIGHT and unmerged. Any checklist item or loop step\n   that depends on them must say so and name the issue, not read as available.\n   Same for anything needing 1.6 (`condition` halting) or 2d9a1da (sampling) —\n   those are named as blocked in places already; check the coverage is complete.\n\nVERDICTS, one per finding, in the shape `2f2796e` established:\nCONFIRMED / CORRECTED / UNVERIFIABLE-FROM-SOURCE / INFERENCE-UNMARKED.\nComment findings on the owning issue (96d9315 for 4.1, d2e1229 for 4.2). Change\nno files — the orchestrator applies corrections after reading the verdicts.\n\nONE KNOWN GAP TO CONFIRM RATHER THAN REDISCOVER: `accept/4.2-play-loop.py` has\nnever been run — BORGES has no Python, which is why this repo's other drivers\nare `.ps1`. Its author says it is desk-checked only and asks for its `--selftest`\nto be 